<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Castillo San Cristóbal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1634–1783</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Castillo San Cristóbal is a Spanish fortress in Old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-juan-puerto-rico">San Juan, Puerto Rico</a>, built mainly between 1634 and 1783 to defend the city against attack by land. Covering some eleven hectares, it was the largest fortification built by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>. Together with El Morro it repelled the British assault of 1797, and it is now part of the San Juan National Historic Site.</p></div>
